  <language>fr_FR</language>
  <keyword>isregular</keyword>
  <short_description>Teste si des valeurs datetime sont regulierement espacees.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>tf = isregular(t)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>tf = isregular(t, unit)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>inputs</param_name>
      <param_description>Un tableau datetime et un selecteur optionnel comme years, quarters, months, weeks ou days.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output</param_name>
      <param_description>Un scalaire logique.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Teste si des valeurs datetime sont regulierement espacees.</p>
    <p>Sans unite, la regularite est testee sur les differences de dates serie. Avec une unite calendaire, la fonction compare les indices d unite.</p>
    <p>Array-valued inputs keep their data shape when the operation supports arrays. Scalar operands are expanded where the implementation defines scalar expansion.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Utilisation de base.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[isregular(datetime(2024,1,1):days(1):datetime(2024,1,3))
isregular([datetime(2024,1,1), datetime(2024,2,1), datetime(2024,3,1)], 'months')
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
